   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 2^{x} \\) and \\( \\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3} \\), so the product rule comes first: \\( f'(x) = \\left(2^{x}\\right)'\\,\\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3} + 2^{x}\\left(\\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3}\\right)' \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               2,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Sin",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        2,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ],
                  1
               ],
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 2^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 2^{x} \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               2,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3} \\) is a cube of \\( 1 + \\sin(2x) \\), which contains a sine of \\( 2x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\left(1 + \\sin(2x)\\right)^{3}\\right)' = 6 \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 1\\right)^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            6,
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Sin",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        2,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ],
                  1
               ],
               2
            ],
            [
               "Cos",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Assemble the product rule and evaluate at \\( x = 0 \\): \\( f'(0) = \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 6 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ],
            6
         ]
      }
